# GitHub Scrum board
Board: Project 1 "QA-lab URL Review" (https://github.com/orgs/carlosandmunoz-hq/projects/1), repo `kaanmuar/kaanmuar.github.io`. Columns: Backlog, Next, Design, Dev, QA, Stg, Prod, Done. All board chores via `scripts/ticket.sh` (`new`, `bug`, `design`, `move`, `child`, `done`, `log`).

- **Ticket every piece of work.** Find it, or `scripts/ticket.sh new "<title>" <area> dev` (`kind:request` + one `area:*`). Move as work moves; cite in the PR body.
- **Findings while developing are their own issues** (bug, regression, incongruence, process slip), even if fixed in the same PR. `scripts/ticket.sh bug <ticket> "BE: …" <area> "<what>" "<fix>" [fixed-pr]` links a sub-issue and closes Done with the PR or leaves Backlog. `new`/`bug` list likely dupes (#2969); use `--dry-run` first, comment on a match, or `--no-dup-check` once none match.
- URL-review failure-cause fixes: add a `FIXES` row in `functions/url-review-failures.js` (cause, merge time, PR) so covered runs re-run.
- **Design deliverables** (templates, layouts, images, logos, icons, share images, social, motion, copy/visual changes and later updates): `scripts/ticket.sh design <ticket> "Design: ..." "<decisions, paths, live link>"`; Done when shipped.

## GitHub API budget
Chats share kaanmuar's 5,000 GraphQL points/hour (#892). `gh issue`/`pr`/`pr checks`/`project` spend it.
- Issues/comments/labels/sub-issues: REST (`gh api`), as `ticket.sh` does.
- CI: `scripts/ci-wait.sh <sha|pr>` only—never `gh pr checks --watch`.
- Main fixed, PRs still red: `scripts/refresh-prs.sh [workflow]` (close/reopen). Never `gh run rerun` on the PR's failed jobs (#2245: old merge commit).
- PRs: `gh api repos/kaanmuar/kaanmuar.github.io/pulls -f title=... -f head=<branch> -f base=main -f body=...`; merge `gh api -X PUT .../pulls/<n>/merge -f merge_method=squash`.
- Board moves only via `scripts/gh-budget.sh` (qa-lab-agents first)—`ticket.sh` uses it.
